# Workers Assets serves static files before the Worker runs, so headers cannot
# be set in code — this file is the only place they can be set.
#
# The HTML must never come from a cache. It is the file that decides which
# versioned script runs, so a stale copy pins the whole app to an old build
# while every later deploy lands correctly and invisibly. That is exactly what
# happened here: the API reported the new build and the page kept running the
# old one, which looks identical to the deploy not working at all.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
